  "findings": [
    "All 15 frozen heading-word obligations are fully contained and visually complete. Andante, Menuetto, Trio and Rondo/Allegretto appear at their correct source systems and matching horizontal locations.",
    "Clarinet output page 6 displays Rondo/Allegretto twice. The complete source glyphs already fit in the main crop; 0.33407857160137 points of additional top padding in the recognized heading caused a second copied rectangle. Other Clarinet headings occur once.",
    "Copied Menuetto, Trio and Rondo/Allegretto retain small slur fragments below the word. The fragments do not cut the heading glyphs or overprint the target staff.",
    "All 39 page overviews were inspected. No new overlap, page overflow, blank page or mostly empty final page was observed. The added direction space increases Piano from 17 to 18 pages; final page 18 has 8 systems and is sensibly filled.",
    "The frozen first/second-ending bracket region at source page 25, system 3 is still absent from Viola output 9 and Piano 16. Clarinet 10 preserves both endings.",
    "Main crop geometry is identical across all 405 bands; existing sliced neighboring notation and previous-system fragments persist, including Clarinet 10. Movement starts/page turns remain unoptimized."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Experimental recognizer remains outside app default.",
    "The duplicate Clarinet Rondo heading is a quality defect; this report does not treat complete glyph containment as a clean output pass.",
    "The lower-part ending-bracket obligations remain unresolved, and other shared directions have not been exhaustively inventoried."
  ]
}
